  "nl_text": "The rschema_0350 database contains eight tables that are used to store information about a conference. The Ticket_Type table contains information about the different types of tickets that can be purchased for the conference, including the name, description, price, and whether or not it includes a workshop. The Discount_Code table contains information about the different discount codes that can be used to get a discount on the cost of a ticket, including the name, type, and amount of the discount. The Meeting table contains information about the different meetings that will be held during the conference, including the date, time, location, and description. The Workshop table contains information about the different workshops that will be held during the conference, including the date, time, location, and description. The Speaker table contains information about the different speakers who will be giving presentations during the conference, including their name, company, and bio. The Participant table contains information about the different participants who will be attending the conference, including their name, company, email, and discount code. The Meeting_Speaker table contains information about the speakers who will be giving presentations at each meeting, including the meeting and speaker. The Workshop_Speaker table contains information about the speakers who will be giving presentations at each workshop, including the workshop and speaker.",
  "gold_question": "The design of a technology conference management system is as follows:\nThe conference has participants, whose information includes Participant ID, Name, Company, and Email.\nThe conference offers various types of tickets, with ticket information including Ticket ID, Name, Description, Price, and whether it includes workshops, with each participant limited to purchasing one ticket.\nParticipants can use discount codes to purchase tickets, with discount code information including Code, Name, Type, and Amount.\nAfter purchasing tickets, participant ticket records are generated, containing Participant ID, Ticket ID, Discount Code ID, and Net Price.\nThe conference schedules multiple meetings, with meeting information including Name, Description, Date, Start Time, End Time, and Room.\nFurthermore, the conference also offers workshops, with workshop information including Name, Description, Requirements, Location, Date, Start Time, End Time, and Capacity.\nEach meeting or workshop can have multiple speakers, with speaker information including Name, Company, and Description.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0350.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0350\nCREATE TABLE `ticket_type` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `includes_workshop` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `discount_code` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `meeting` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `time` time NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `workshop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `time` time NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `speaker` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `company` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `bio` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `participant` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `company` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `discount_code_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `participant_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`discount_code_id`) REFERENCES `discount_code` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `meeting_speaker` (\n  `meeting_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `speaker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meeting_id`, `speaker_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `meeting_speaker_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`meeting_id`) REFERENCES `meeting` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `meeting_speaker_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`speaker_id`) REFERENCES `speaker` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `workshop_speaker` (\n  `workshop_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `speaker_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`workshop_id`, `speaker_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `workshop_speaker_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`workshop_id`) REFERENCES `workshop` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `workshop_speaker_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`speaker_id`) REFERENCES `speaker` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
